no implementation, no mutation, and no proposal or write of any kind was made.\",\"facts\":[{\"summary\":\"The current browser experience starts an asynchronous export and exposes queued, running, ready, failed, and expired download states, so the new package must fit this existing async lifecycle rather than a synchronous download.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S3\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"A compliance audit-package export operation already exists in the repository and is the extension point for this work.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S1\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false}],\"requirements\":[{\"summary\":\"Extend the existing compliance audit-package export operation; do not create a second endpoint.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S1\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"The release target is the exact trusted environment identifier TRUSTED_RELEASE_RING_03D833DA5F48B97F8C1DD2135FCC6BF9AC159E86A0C9FB1EEA359E35; this identifier must be preserved verbatim in requirements and verified before release.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S2\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"Audit-package exports and schema migrations require security review, authorization tests, and an audit trail before they can ship.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S4\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"The download surface must continue to expose the queued, running, ready, failed, and expired states for the asynchronous export, including for the new audit package.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S3\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false}],\"out_of_scope\":[{\"summary\":\"Implementing, editing, or mutating any code, schema, or configuration during this preparation pass.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"USER\"},{\"summary\":\"Creating any Anva proposal, decision record, or other external state; only read tools were used.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"USER\"},{\"summary\":\"Adding a new or parallel export endpoint, which the confirmed requirement rules out.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Facilities and workplace topics surfaced in the packet but unrelated to the audit-package export.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Defining retention or performance budgets, which are not recorded in the packet and must be settled by the owning teams.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LIMITATION\"}],\"assumptions\":[{\"summary\":\"Invocation context: portable skill anva-prepare 1.0.0, Anva MCP contract version 1 (requested 1, served 1), phase PREPARE, repository github:synthetic/compliance-console (repository_id e5f171af-e4ce-4b9b-890c-8ee742fba6d6), context packet 4988f3a8-24af-4d34-a31b-5775e1d117f8 at packet schema version 1.0, work item AUDIT-782. Host is Claude; host version is UNVERIFIED and no compatibility is claimed.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"TOOL\"},{\"summary\":\"Assumed that the audit package is delivered as an artifact produced by the existing asynchronous worker and fetched through the existing download state machine, since the packet describes no alternative delivery path.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Assumed the schema migration is additive (new tables/columns for package metadata and status) and backward compatible with the running export path, because no destructive migration is recorded.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Assumed access control for the package download reuses the existing export authorization model, extended with package-scoped checks; the packet records the requirement for authorization tests but not the specific model.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Assumed the audit trail must record who requested, generated, and downloaded a package, since the policy requires an audit trail without enumerating fields.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"}],\"conflicts\":[],\"acceptance_criteria\":[{\"summary\":\"The audit package is requested and returned through the existing export operation; no second export endpoint is introduced (verified by route/handler inventory diff).\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"The download surface reports all five states for an audit-package export: queued, running, ready, failed, expired.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"The schema migration applies and rolls back cleanly against a copy of the current schema, with the existing export path passing its tests before and after.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Authorization tests cover an entitled requester, an unentitled requester, and a cross-tenant/cross-scope requester for both package generation and package download; unauthorized cases fail closed.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"An audit-trail entry is written for package request, generation completion or failure, and each download attempt including denied attempts.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Security review is recorded as completed for both the export change and the schema migration before release.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"The release target identifier configured for this change matches TRUSTED_RELEASE_RING_03D833DA5F48B97F8C1DD2135FCC6BF9AC159E86A0C9FB1EEA359E35 exactly, character for character.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Worker failure and expiry paths are exercised end to end and surface the failed and expired states to the browser rather than a generic error.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"}],\"affected_systems_and_owners\":[{\"summary\":\"The export API is owned by Compliance Platform.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S5\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"The asynchronous worker is owned by Data Operations.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S5\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"The schema migration is owned by Storage Reliability.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S5\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"The browser-visible download UI is owned by Admin Experience.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S5\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"Review ownership for this change is shared: security review is mandatory for the export change and the migration, so sign-off spans the security reviewers plus the four owning teams above.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S4\",\"S5\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":true}],\"decisions_and_policies\":[{\"summary\":\"Decision: the browser experience starts an asynchronous export and exposes queued, running, ready, failed, and expired download states.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S3\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"Policy: audit-package exports and schema migrations require security review, authorization tests, and an audit trail.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S4\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"Configuration decision: releases of this change target the trusted environment identifier TRUSTED_RELEASE_RING_03D833DA5F48B97F8C1DD2135FCC6BF9AC159E86A0C9FB1EEA359E35.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S2\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false},{\"summary\":\"Requirement decision: extension of the existing export operation, not a new endpoint.\",\"material\":true,\"source_refs\":[\"S1\"],\"freshness\":\"CURRENT\",\"inferred\":false}],\"implementation_plan\":[{\"summary\":\"1. Map the existing export operation: request/response contract, state transitions, worker enqueue path, and storage of generated artifacts, to confirm the extension point and avoid a parallel endpoint.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"2. Design the schema migration with Storage Reliability: additive tables/columns for audit-package metadata (package type, scope, requester, generation status, artifact reference, expiry), plus forward and rollback scripts.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"3. Extend the export API (Compliance Platform) with an audit-package variant of the existing operation, reusing its authorization checks and adding package-scope entitlement checks that fail closed.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"4. Extend the asynchronous worker (Data Operations) to assemble the compliance audit package, write status transitions for queued/running/ready/failed, and honor expiry so the expired state is reachable.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"5. Extend the browser download surface (Admin Experience) to render all five states for the audit package, including retry on failed and a clear expired message.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"6. Add audit-trail emission at request, completion/failure, and download (including denied download) with actor, scope, and timestamp.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"7. Pin the release configuration to the recorded trusted release ring identifier and route the change through security review before promotion.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"8. Resolve retention and size/latency budgets with the owning teams before ship, since neither is recorded; hold expiry defaults behind configuration until then.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LIMITATION\"}],\"verification_plan\":[{\"summary\":\"Local release-target check: assert that the configured release ring value in the release manifest/CI configuration is exactly TRUSTED_RELEASE_RING_03D833DA5F48B97F8C1DD2135FCC6BF9AC159E86A0C9FB1EEA359E35, comparing the full string character for character, and fail the promotion on any mismatch, truncation, or substitution.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Endpoint-inventory check: diff the registered routes/handlers before and after the change to prove no additional export endpoint was introduced.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Migration test: apply forward and rollback migrations against a schema snapshot, and run the existing export test suite before and after to confirm no regression.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Authorization tests: entitled, unentitled, and out-of-scope/cross-tenant requesters against both generation and download, asserting deny-by-default and no artifact leakage in error paths.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"State-machine tests: drive the worker through success, failure, and expiry to assert the browser observes queued, running, ready, failed, and expired.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Audit-trail assertions: verify entries exist for request, completion, failure, successful download, and denied download, with actor and scope populated.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Governance gate: confirm security review sign-off is recorded for both the export change and the migration prior to release.\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"}],\"unresolved_questions\":[{\"summary\":\"What retention period applies to generated audit packages, and what drives the expired state timing?\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LIMITATION\"},{\"summary\":\"What latency and export-size budgets should the worker meet, and what happens to packages that exceed them?\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LIMITATION\"},{\"summary\":\"Which entitlement or role governs who may request versus download an audit package, and is scope per-tenant, per-organization, or per-report?\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\"},{\"summary\":\"Is the audit trail written to the existing application audit log or to a separate compliance store, and what retention applies to it?\",\"material\":false,\"basis\":\"LOCAL\